battlefield 2042's launch is so close  and yet there's something oddly missing  from the flurry of details trailers  previews and betas that have come out  recently the missing piece is hazard  zone the squad-based all-new game mode  to the battlefield franchise dice just  dropped his trailer showing the new  hazard zone and we've got all the  details spoiler alert it's a lot less  battle royale and a lot more division  style dark zone a quick note is that we  don't have a lot of footage of hazard  zone other than the official trailer so  most gameplay you'll see is from the all  out warfare beta do me a solid and hit  that like button and subscribe because  we have battlefield 2042 live streams  beta breakdowns gameplay and so much  more on the channel and you won't want  to miss a thing  battlefield hazard zone is not a battle  royale trust me dice really wants you to  know this they've been adamant about it  from the beginning what we have instead  is a smaller 24 or 32 player lobby with  multiple squads the objective is simple  strategize retrieve and extract you and  your squad are basically a group of  notepad specialists that are tasked with  securing valuable intel on each map  you're fighting other squads in time and  the terrain you have limited time to  secure the intel and make it to an  aircraft and you can do this repeatedly  with the risk increasing each time  multiple squads have the same objective  so you need to decide if it is worth  fighting or avoiding each other squat  fights are merely a byproduct of your  true goal of simply securing the downed  satellite's data i'm not entirely sure  but i think that there will be ai  enemies as well our preview briefing  mentioned that occupying forces are also  a threat this leads me to believe that  ai us or russian forces will be  defending certain satellites if the ai  is involved  that could be a problem judging from  just how goofy they were during the beta  but we'll have to wait and see what i  know about the occupying forces is that  they will acquire targets quickly and  they will focus on self-preservation  according to dice prolonged engagements  with them mean potential draining of  your resources not to mention all that  ruckus will potentially grab the  attention of a nearby squad hazard  zone's gameplay will consist of 24  players on last gen consoles while  series x and s ps5 and pc owners will be  in lobbies of up to 32 players tornadoes  will also drop down at random adding to  the tension if you go down you will  still have a shot at living to fight  another day by crawling to safety being  killed while you're down however will  place you on a spectator screen squad  mates can still get you back in the  fight using a reinforcement uplink found  scattered across the map or as a  tactical upgrade purchasable with dark  market credits more on the tactical  upgrades in the credits in just a bit  though finally hazard zone will be  playable on all of the launch maps  confirmed for all out warfare including  orbital manifest hourglass and more  there will only be two extraction zones  one early on and one at the end of the  match and both zones will be in  different locations this means that only  two squads will make it out alive or  potentially none at all a match will  most likely go like this before each  game your squad will be briefed with a  predetermined starting zone that will  kick off your match's first phase which  is strategize and equip based on the map  in your starting zone your squad will  decide which specialist to use what  weapons and equipment you'll need and  the overall game plan specialists will  be locked to one player so no army of  boris's or falx instead you'll have to  appropriately synergize and consider the  team composition working with each  specialist advantage or disadvantages  once you load in it is time to start the  retrieval and to search for data drives  an intel scanner is a unique hazard zone  gadget that will help you track down the  location of these data drives you will  definitely want to make sure one squad  member has that intel scanner because  that device will be essential to your  objective this leads you into the mid  game where new satellites will continue  to fall from the sky with more encrypted  data drives these satellites will be  even more valuable than those from the  early match being defended by the  occupying forces at this point you're  forced to make a decision do you take  the first extraction opportunity which  will open up halfway through the match  if you decide to play it safe and  extract now you will need to dip asap  and fight any other early squats to  board a waiting condor however if you're  the type to go for broke you'll be  rewarded for your confidence assuming  you're able to make it out alive these  squads will have to go for the second  and final extraction which is obviously  riskier since any remaining units will  be going for the same goal as you fight  over the final extraction zone with your  team if you fall behind and miss the  extraction you will lose everything you  acquired in the match however if a  single squad member manages to board the  condor the entire squad will be rewarded  so what exactly are the rewards they  come in the form of dark market credits  which you secure from extracting the  data these credits are only usable in  hazard zone and purchases will lead to  specific tactical upgrades there will be  two free upgrades like starting with  plus 20 armor or getting 50 additional  credits for kills and occupying forces  some examples of dark market tactical  upgrades are quick draw holster this  will let you switch weapons 15 faster  while another upgrade like faster  healing gives you a 20 boost to health  regeneration how many credits you get  depend on the data drives that you've  extracted each data drive has an  assigned value with later satellites  potentially having the higher value  drives dice refers to the dark market as  the first component of the metagame the  more tactical upgrades you have the  greater the chance of a successful round  the other parts of this meta involve  passive upgrades your loadout and your  extraction streak the extraction streak  is a level attached to each unique  specialist you play a successful round  increases your streak by one and failure  resets your streak back to zero but if  you're able to get a good streak going  you will be rewarded with discounts when  purchasing tactical upgrades or loadout  items so hazard zone is definitely not a  battle royale they were really right  about that it does though feel similar  to my experience playing the division's  dark zone except way more team based i'm  curious how balanced the dark market  might be or if new squads have a  fighting chance against souped-up teams  with the best upgrades only time will  tell and those of you with early access  will get your shot at the mode on  november 12th all other players will be  able to dive into hazard zone with  battlefield 2042's launch on november  19th let me know if you're excited about  hazard zone or still thinking about the  open beta that wrapped up we've got our  thoughts on the good the bad and the  ugly from what we've seen so far in  another video so stick to gamespot for  all things battlefield until next time  [Music]
 

